# ─── Typed Node list for a Linux host Server ─────────────────────────
#
# Optional. When ${FLOWTREE_AGENT_HOME}/nodes.properties exists (or
# FLOWTREE_AGENT_NODES names another file), install.sh appends it to the
# installed conf/agent.properties, so one host Server runs every Node listed
# here. Without it the Server builds the legacy homogeneous group of native
# Nodes, exactly like the macOS agent.
#
# Index is the node id; indices must be contiguous from 0. Labels are
# per Node and are not broadcast to siblings. A native Node takes the host's
# platform and hostname labels automatically; a container Node takes its
# platform from this file, because that is a property of its image.
#
# The `runtime` labels below are what the end-to-end smoke (smoke.sh)
# routes its two jobs by; keep them, or pass smoke.sh the labels you use.
#
# kind=docker needs the Docker Node kind, which is a later addition to the
# runtime: on a build without it the Server rejects the unknown kind at
# startup and install.sh reports that the agent did not connect. install.sh
# also refuses to install a docker Node unless `docker info` works for the
# service account.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

nodes.0.kind=native
nodes.0.labels.runtime=native

nodes.1.kind=docker
nodes.1.labels.runtime=docker
nodes.1.labels.platform=linux
nodes.1.image=flowtree/agent:latest
nodes.1.cpus=4
nodes.1.memory=4g
